WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.912
This slide brings the entire workflow together.

00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:06.827
Start with a question. Bring in external data.

00:00:06.827 --> 00:00:11.427
Inspect and clean it. Define features and the target.

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:14.497
Split into training and test sets.

00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:18.547
Fit the model. Evaluate it against a baseline.

00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:21.432
Then use the fitted model for new predictions.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:27.302
The Python example demonstrates the core technical stages using a Pipeline.

00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:32.032
But a real machine learning project continues beyond one notebook.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:36.512
Models need monitoring. Data distributions can change.

00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:40.867
Performance can drift. New data may require retraining.

00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:47.092
Privacy, fairness, documentation, and operational constraints also matter.

00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:50.867
For now, focus on recognizing the structure.

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:58.324
If you understand this workflow, you already have the conceptual map you need for a much deeper machine learning course.
